cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this library in work you publish, cite it as below."
title: "hrt-pk-core: an offline pharmacokinetic engine for estradiol and testosterone HRT"
abstract: >-
  A Rust library that turns a list of doses and blood tests into concentration
  curves for estradiol, testosterone and cyproterone acetate, and answers
  questions about those curves: peak, trough, time-weighted mean, AUC, time in
  range, steady state, the dose that reaches a target, falling crossings for
  reminders, adherence and supply forecasts, and unit conversion between mass
  and molar concentrations. It is distributed as a shared library behind a
  JSON-over-C ABI, with bindings for Dart, Python and .NET, and builds for
  Android, iOS, Windows, macOS and Linux. It performs no I/O: no network, no
  clock, no filesystem.
type: software
